Day 96 – Schema Design

Task:
Design document structure
👉 Build:
Blog schema (title, content, author)


Sample document:
{
  "title": "MongoDB Basics",
  "content": "Learning MongoDB",
  "author": "Shivam",
  "likes": 10
}

CREATE Queries
1. Insert One Blog
db.blogs.insertOne({
  title: "MongoDB Basics",
  content: "Learning MongoDB",
  author: "Shivam"
})

2. Insert Multiple Blogs
db.blogs.insertMany([
  {
    title: "MongoDB Basics",
    content: "Learning MongoDB",
    author: "Shivam"
  },
  {
    title: "NoSQL",
    content: "MongoDB is NoSQL",
    author: "Rahul"
  }
])
READ Queries

3. Show All Blogs
db.blogs.find()

4. Find One Blog
db.blogs.findOne({ author: "Shivam" })

5. Find by Title
db.blogs.find({ title: "MongoDB Basics" })

6. Find by Author
db.blogs.find({ author: "Rahul" })

7. Find with Likes > 5
db.blogs.find({ likes: { $gt: 5 } })
UPDATE Queries

8. Update One Blog
db.blogs.updateOne(
  { author: "Shivam" },
  { $set: { author: "Shivam Raj" } }
)

9. Update Likes
db.blogs.updateOne(
  { title: "MongoDB Basics" },
  { $set: { likes: 50 } }
)

10. Add New Field
db.blogs.updateMany(
  {},
  { $set: { category: "Database" } }
)
DELETE Queries

11. Delete One Blog
db.blogs.deleteOne({
  title: "NoSQL"
})

12. Delete Multiple Blogs
db.blogs.deleteMany({
  author: "Rahul"
})

SORT Queries
13. Sort by Likes Ascending
db.blogs.find().sort({ likes: 1 })

14. Sort by Likes Descending
db.blogs.find().sort({ likes: -1 })

LIMIT Queries
15. Show First 2 Blogs
db.blogs.find().limit(2)
COUNT Queries

16. Count Blogs
db.blogs.countDocuments()

SEARCH Queries
17. Blogs by Category
db.blogs.find({
  category: "Database"
})

18. Find Blogs with Specific Word
db.blogs.find({
  title: /Mongo/
})

DROP Queries
19. Delete Collection
db.blogs.drop()